  "description": "NLog is a logging platform for .NET with rich log routing and management capabilities.\nNLog supports traditional logging, structured logging and the combination of both.\n\nSupported platforms:\n\n- .NET 5, 6, 7, 8 and 9\n- .NET Core 1, 2 and 3\n- .NET Standard 1.3+ and 2.0+\n- .NET Framework 3.5 - 4.8\n- Xamarin Android + iOS (.NET Standard)\n- Mono 4\n\nFor ASP.NET Core, check: https://www.nuget.org/packages/NLog.Web.AspNetCore",
  "iconFile": "N.png",
  "id": "NLog",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2025-05-29T08:42:26.957Z",
  "licenseExpression": "BSD-3-Clause",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/BSD-3-Clause",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "yymACERmJN27ztQ3b8DzoApIBjJPSRm67VOQIGX7VByRqA7ZDh7vwETCOJmUHqVvyhwX1bxZA5Sl9CQPoQ59CQ==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 2981540,
  "projectUrl": "https://nlog-project.org/",
  "published": "2025-05-29T08:39:14.803Z",
  "releaseNotes": "ChangeLog:\n- Restored LogFactory.Setup().SetupFromEnvironmentVariables() as not obsolete (#5710) @snakefoot\n- Avoid using MakeGenericType for Dictionary enumeration when AOT (#5717) @snakefoot\n- Stop using obsolete Assembly.CodeBase for NetStandard (#5730) @snakefoot\n- ExceptionLayoutRenderer - Handle Exception properties like StackTrace can throw with AOT (#5742) @snakefoot\n- ExceptionLayoutRenderer - Handle Data-collection-item ToString can throw with AOT (#5743) @snakefoot\n- ExceptionLayoutRenderer - Handle Exception-properties can throw with AOT (#5763) @snakefoot\n- ServiceRepository - Improve exception-handling when resolving service-types while disposing (#5756) @snakefoot\n- LayoutRenderer - Optimize performance by skipping cache result from render Inner Layout (#5759) @snakefoot\n- ConditionLayoutExpression  - Optimize performance by skipping cache result from render Inner Layout (#5795) @snakefoot\n- Mark IFactory RegisterType as obsolete, since it will be removed with NLog v6 (#5731) @snakefoot\n- Mark JsonLayout EscapeForwardSlash as obsolete, since disabled with NLog v6 (#5766) @snakefoot\n- Mark ExceptionLayoutRenderer Formats-List as obsolete, since immutable with NLog v6 (#5823) @snakefoot\n- Updated API-code examples to not depend on obsolete SimpleConfigurator (#5769) @snakefoot\n- ObjectReflectionCache - Handle PropertyValue can throw with AOT (#5776) @snakefoot\n- NetworkTarget - Introduced option NoDelay to disable delayed ACK (#5780) @snakefoot\n- Fix InternalLogger noise about reflection for FuncLayoutRenderer (#5788) @snakefoot\n- TargetWithContext - Reduce allocation for RenderLogEvent when SimpleLayout (#5792) @snakefoot\n- Refactoring to improve null value handling (#5810) @snakefoot\n- Refactoring to improve null value handling (#5812) @snakefoot\n- LoggingConfigurationParser - Prioritize LoggingRules from current config (#5817) @snakefoot\n- WhenEmptyLayoutRendererWrapper - Optimize IStringValueRenderer Logic (#5825) @snakefoot\n\nNLog v5.2 changes how to load extensions: https://nlog-project.org/2023/05/30/nlog-5-2-trim-warnings.html\n\nList of major changes in NLog 5.0: https://nlog-project.org/2022/05/16/nlog-5-0-finally-ready.html\n\nFull changelog: https://github.com/NLog/NLog/releases\n\nFor all config options and platform support, check https://nlog-project.org/config/",
